{
  "note": "The reviewed-controls assembly of the OSCAL 1.2.1 assessment-results model. It requires control-selections, and each selection must carry either include-all or include-controls. So the requirement that a result declare the controls it reviewed can be satisfied with include-all, without naming any one control. The single assessment result in the three bodies of content does exactly that.",
  "model": "assessment-results",
